      {
        "id": "513502",
        "date_added": "2026-10-23 04:10:44",
        "twitter_handle": null,
        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "Full-chain lure with ONLY the ~1.02 GB junk region removed: loader (= 58dffd262bb9b3c815f1017735cfa214fbbb029af8bd4cbba42c3d8db218e582) + ChaCha20 payload + 896-byte pad + 64-byte footer. The loader locates the payload relative to end-of-file, so this should run like the 1 GB original (inference; my static re-decryption of this file yields the identical stage 2 9933977b38adbe73cc852ffca785c4111b7922de7e515801ec8411e9e25708ce). Untested in a sandbox. Fake TV-episode torrent campaign (LimeTorrents; 'MobLand S02E06 A Different Corner 1080p WEB H264-CAKES.7z', also seen as Tulsa King S04E02 and VisionQuest S01E05). Outer ZIP-named-.7z sha256 ad4ab37a14f0e80e8d2d2109d3a980718ddb58583da530ec5311252a5c9514bb holds vlc-3.0.23-win64_crypted.exe (1,023,025,653 bytes, sha256 53c889d81914869958a2662518706e4f4dc47a22f380599c2967ea4b5d39288d). Same campaign as Thereallo's South Park S29E03 analysis (thereallo.dev). Footer layout from that write-up confirmed on this build: fnv1a32(.data[0:32]) = footer[0x3C] = 0xec378ff9, flags 3, payload 1,313,792 bytes, padding 896; layout [loader 128000][~1.02 GB junk][ChaCha20 payload][896 pad][64 B footer]; key = footer[0:32] XOR mask, counter 0. "
      }
